Round 1, read as laid out (6 and 12 PDF pages) by three fictional readers, test instruments: a conference team member with their own agent, a newsroom builder, a first-build finisher. All three got the factory in both editions; all three would start tomorrow from the 3-page edition, only "maybe" from the 10-page one (yes from its draft): the action page comes late and the pages before it read unfinished.

Yours, page by page:
1. Pages 3, 4 and 8 (10): the pictures, cast cards and strips are described in italic stage directions but not drawn; draw them, or take the directions off the printed page. Start with one picture of the factory's nine stations (all three).
2. Most scene pages (10: pages 5, 7, 9, 10): more than half the sheet empty; fill with a cast card for each speaker, or a clock strip (midnight, 05:00, 14:00, 18:44), or merge pages (all three).
3. Page 5 (03): the four steps as numbered cards, like the ten's page 11, the page all three call the best.
4. Page 1 (03, 10): the cover is a bare title; with the storyteller's promise line, perhaps the cast as a row.

